Are you doing this to pressure me?

6
00:00:17,860 --> 00:00:20,100
I have to protect our hotel’s interests.

7
00:00:20,590 --> 00:00:21,580
This is my fault.

8
00:00:21,970 --> 00:00:23,500
I’m the reason you are sick.

9
00:00:23,960 --> 00:00:24,930
It’s your fault.

10
00:00:25,840 --> 00:00:26,860
It’s all your fault, Key.

11
00:00:26,890 --> 00:00:28,200
Everyone will die because of you.

12
00:00:28,300 --> 00:00:30,530
Key used to have bad dreams
when she was young.

13
00:00:30,850 --> 00:00:33,570
Every time she has this dream,
she always runs away.

14
00:00:34,090 --> 00:00:35,980
Is there anything we can do to help Key?

15
00:01:10,289 --> 00:01:11,980
I think we should call the police.

16
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:13,850
Yes.

17
00:01:20,380 --> 00:01:21,270
Miss Key.

18
00:01:22,130 --> 00:01:23,050
Hello, Key.

19
00:01:23,630 --> 00:01:25,200
Where are you? Are you okay?

20
00:01:28,660 --> 00:01:29,700
Peach.

21
00:01:31,250 --> 00:01:33,200
Are you with Dad and Big Mom?

22
00:01:35,220 --> 00:01:37,180
Yes, everyone is here.

23
00:01:37,220 --> 00:01:38,380
Aunt Niam is also here.

24
00:01:39,800 --> 00:01:41,400
Can you put me on speaker?

25
00:01:42,580 --> 00:01:44,500
I want to talk to everyone.

26
00:01:45,810 --> 00:01:46,500
Sure.

27
00:01:52,630 --> 00:01:54,900
Key, where are you?

28
00:01:55,110 --> 00:01:56,600
Are you safe?

29
00:01:56,890 --> 00:02:00,300
I’m safe, Big Mom.

30
00:02:03,900 --> 00:02:05,100
Honey, please come home.

31
00:02:06,920 --> 00:02:08,380
Key, where are you?

32
00:02:08,639 --> 00:02:10,130
Can you tell me?

33
00:02:12,330 --> 00:02:14,200
Don’t worry about me.

34
00:02:16,610 --> 00:02:18,600
I just need some time.

35
00:02:23,030 --> 00:02:26,200
When I am stronger,

36
00:02:28,190 --> 00:02:29,800
I will go back.

37
00:02:33,720 --> 00:02:34,600
Okay.

38
00:02:35,570 --> 00:02:37,300
Have you talked to Chan?

39
00:02:42,300 --> 00:02:43,400
Peach.

40
00:02:44,900 --> 00:02:46,530
Can you not tell Chan that I called?

41
00:02:49,490 --> 00:02:50,500
I…

42
00:02:53,200 --> 00:02:55,000
I don’t want her

43
00:02:56,230 --> 00:02:57,700
to see me like this.

44
00:02:59,100 --> 00:02:59,970
(Fine.)

45
00:03:00,940 --> 00:03:04,280
If something happens,
you need to call me immediately, alright?

46
00:03:07,050 --> 00:03:07,870
Yes.

47
00:05:39,260 --> 00:05:42,300
(The number you have dialed
cannot be reached at the moment.)

48
00:06:02,110 --> 00:06:03,760
This is the document for today’s meeting.

49
00:06:06,080 --> 00:06:07,330
I can’t find Key.

50
00:06:09,690 --> 00:06:11,400
I sent more people to look for her.

51
00:06:12,130 --> 00:06:13,170
Thanks, Phu.

52
00:06:13,980 --> 00:06:15,500
Don’t you have any place in mind

53
00:06:15,940 --> 00:06:17,200
that she might be?

54
00:06:27,470 --> 00:06:29,730
Game, cancel today’s meeting.

55
00:06:30,740 --> 00:06:31,500
Yes.

56
00:06:32,830 --> 00:06:33,800
Where are you going?

57
00:06:35,400 --> 00:06:36,500
I’m going to look for Key.

58
00:06:52,700 --> 00:06:55,170
Sun, can you take care of the hotel
while I’m away?

59
00:06:55,210 --> 00:06:57,400
I already assigned Game
to take care of my work.

60
00:06:57,740 --> 00:07:00,700
But if anything comes up,
you can make the decision for me.

61
00:07:00,800 --> 00:07:02,200
(Where are you going?)

62
00:07:03,020 --> 00:07:04,300
I’m going to look for Key.

63
00:07:04,550 --> 00:07:07,240
(Do you know where she is?)

64
00:07:11,040 --> 00:07:12,600
I have a place in mind.

65
00:07:13,520 --> 00:07:14,900
I’m going there to look for her.

66
00:07:15,330 --> 00:07:18,500
(Alright. I’ll take care of the hotel.)

67
00:07:18,790 --> 00:07:20,200
(You can go look for her.)

68
00:07:21,980 --> 00:07:22,900
And…

69
00:07:23,600 --> 00:07:25,300
Can you stop by to look after Simba?

70
00:07:25,650 --> 00:07:26,500
(Sure.)

71
00:07:27,370 --> 00:07:28,400
(Chan.)

72
00:07:29,650 --> 00:07:31,300
(You need to find her…)

73
00:07:32,380 --> 00:07:33,900
(and take her home.)

74
00:07:38,190 --> 00:07:39,900
I’ll do everything to find her.

75
00:08:23,310 --> 00:08:24,500
(Key, do you know this?)

76
00:08:26,780 --> 00:08:28,650
(The moon and the stars,)

77
00:08:31,450 --> 00:08:34,900
(we never see them clearly
on the same night.)

78
00:08:37,490 --> 00:08:38,799
Why?

79
00:08:40,350 --> 00:08:44,640
If we can clearly
see the stars like tonight,

80
00:08:47,090 --> 00:08:50,500
