Key.

157
00:17:20,560 --> 00:17:21,300
Key.

158
00:17:25,040 --> 00:17:27,200
I’m here. I’m right here.

159
00:17:27,579 --> 00:17:28,600
It’s okay.

160
00:17:28,960 --> 00:17:29,900
It’s okay.

161
00:17:30,010 --> 00:17:31,600
Key, look at me.

162
00:17:32,090 --> 00:17:33,000
Look at me.

163
00:17:34,610 --> 00:17:35,500
I’m here.

164
00:18:25,910 --> 00:18:26,700
Sun.

165
00:18:27,370 --> 00:18:29,200
Do you really want to see me?

166
00:18:30,080 --> 00:18:31,100
Yes.

167
00:18:31,420 --> 00:18:33,100
I haven’t seen you for a long time.

168
00:18:33,390 --> 00:18:34,780
Because you are flying around.

169
00:18:34,910 --> 00:18:36,670
You probably lose touch
with all your friends.

170
00:18:36,710 --> 00:18:38,800
What? This is my job.

171
00:18:39,330 --> 00:18:41,030
If I didn’t fly, what else would I do?

172
00:18:41,070 --> 00:18:41,800
Huh?

173
00:18:49,340 --> 00:18:51,500
I saw you look stressed for a while.

174
00:18:52,480 --> 00:18:53,600
What’s wrong?

175
00:18:57,230 --> 00:18:59,100
It’s about my sister’s girlfriend.

176
00:18:59,850 --> 00:19:02,300
What? Your twin has a new girlfriend?

177
00:19:03,170 --> 00:19:04,100
Yes.

178
00:19:04,780 --> 00:19:06,700
Didn’t you see the news?

179
00:19:07,580 --> 00:19:08,380
No.

180
00:19:08,840 --> 00:19:11,000
I don’t read entertainment gossip.

181
00:19:11,700 --> 00:19:14,200
I don’t know your twin personally.

182
00:19:14,950 --> 00:19:16,600
I have never met her.

183
00:19:18,250 --> 00:19:19,100
Why?

184
00:19:19,820 --> 00:19:21,330
Is her new girlfriend not a good person?

185
00:19:22,050 --> 00:19:22,900
She’s nice.

186
00:19:23,250 --> 00:19:24,800
I like her.

187
00:19:25,450 --> 00:19:27,580
But the problem is my mom.

188
00:19:28,080 --> 00:19:29,500
My mom doesn’t like her.

189
00:19:31,630 --> 00:19:32,500
Wait.

190
00:19:33,680 --> 00:19:36,510
You’ve complained to me about
your sister’s girlfriends many times.

191
00:19:36,550 --> 00:19:38,700
This is the first time
that you said her girlfriend is okay.

192
00:19:39,320 --> 00:19:40,900
Unlike when you talk about Jay,

193
00:19:41,390 --> 00:19:42,900
you seem to really hate her.

194
00:19:44,930 --> 00:19:45,900
Of course.

195
00:19:47,130 --> 00:19:49,000
She did a terrible thing to my sister.

196
00:19:49,970 --> 00:19:51,290
It’s hard not to hate her.

197
00:19:53,040 --> 00:19:55,600
I now want to meet this girl, Jay.

198
00:20:07,370 --> 00:20:08,200
Jay.

199
00:20:08,520 --> 00:20:09,580
Wait, Jay.

200
00:20:12,100 --> 00:20:13,400
Why don’t we go to another bar?

201
00:20:13,440 --> 00:20:16,160
No. I’m going to drink here.

202
00:20:18,710 --> 00:20:19,700
Do as you want.

203
00:20:20,420 --> 00:20:22,100
Why are you following me?

204
00:20:22,690 --> 00:20:23,980
I’m worried about you.

205
00:20:25,110 --> 00:20:26,100
Why?

206
00:20:28,230 --> 00:20:29,600
You are my friend.

207
00:20:58,480 --> 00:21:00,300
How dare you come here?

208
00:21:02,250 --> 00:21:04,330
I’m not in the mood
to argue with you today.

209
00:21:04,770 --> 00:21:06,100
Don’t be overreacting.

210
00:21:06,520 --> 00:21:07,800
No, I’m not overreacting.

211
00:21:08,130 --> 00:21:11,500
Backstabbing, that’s your style.

212
00:21:16,490 --> 00:21:18,500
If you're talking about news
about Key’s mom,

213
00:21:18,850 --> 00:21:19,860
I didn’t do it.

214
00:21:19,900 --> 00:21:20,900
Liar.

215
00:21:21,430 --> 00:21:22,700
I said I didn’t do it.

216
00:21:25,340 --> 00:21:27,100
I’m not that coward.

217
00:21:28,190 --> 00:21:29,700
You may not be a coward.

218
00:21:30,210 --> 00:21:32,650
But I think you are a loser.

219
00:21:32,860 --> 00:21:34,300
Watch your mouth, girl.

220
00:21:36,730 --> 00:21:37,800
Girls, stop it.

221
00:21:38,420 --> 00:21:39,400
Calm down.

222
00:21:40,260 --> 00:21:41,100
Sun.

223
00:21:41,520 --> 00:21:43,000
Jay didn’t do it.

224
00:21:43,370 --> 00:21:45,100
Whose side are you taking, Phu?

225
00:21:45,730 --> 00:21:47,150
I’m not taking anyone’s side.

226
00:21:47,620 --> 00:21:51,570
You, Chan, and Jay are my friends.

227
00:21:54,120 --> 00:21:56,330
I just don’t want you guys
to misunderstand each other.

228
00:21:58,990 --> 00:22:04,610
Do you know that your mom asked me
to steal Chan from Key?

229
00:22:05,870 --> 00:22:07,100
But I refused to do it.

230
00:22:08,110 --> 00:22:10,490
Because I have too much
dignity to do that.

231
00:22:12,600 --> 00:22:13,750
Jay is telling the truth.

232
00:22:14,720 --> 00:22:15,810
She didn’t do it.

233
00:22:18,370 --> 00:22:19,600
I can confirm that.

234
00:22:21,060 --> 00:22:23,700
Your mom must think so poorly of Key.

235
00:22:24,230 --> 00:22:27,580
She’d rather see me
get back together with Chan.

236
00:22:28,260 --> 00:22:30,100
Have you asked Chan

237
00:22:31,130 --> 00:22:33,700
if she wants to take you back?

238
00:22:44,130 --> 00:22:45,450
Calm down.

239
00:22:47,540 --> 00:22:49,300
You are a celebrity.

240
00:22:56,140 --> 00:22:57,100
You!

241
00:22:57,390 --> 00:22:58,800
Long time no see.

242
00:23:00,900 --> 00:23:02,700
Don’t get wasted today, Missy.

243
00:23:06,620 --> 00:23:07,400
Elle.

244
00:23:08,280 --> 00:23:09,460
Do you know her?

245
00:23:11,270 --> 00:23:13,000
This is Jay, Chan’s ex?

246
00:23:18,600 --> 00:23:19,400
Jay.

247
00:23:19,740 --> 00:23:20,770
Jay, where are you going?

248
00:23:25,870 --> 00:23:27,700
Now, I want to know about the news.

249
00:23:28,190 --> 00:23:29,300
What happened?

250
00:23:33,820 --> 00:23:36,930
Jay is the ex-girlfriend who dumped Chan.

251
00:23:37,470 --> 00:23:39,580
But actually, she still loves Chan.

252
00:23:39,780 --> 00:23:41,120
So she came back to Chan.

253
00:23:42,680 --> 00:23:44,700
But Chan has already moved on.

254
00:23:44,840 --> 00:23:47,100
She has a new girlfriend named Key.

255
00:23:47,740 --> 00:23:49,570
Everything is
heading toward a happy ending.

256
00:23:50,230 --> 00:23:54,600
Suddenly, scandals
about Key’s family explode.

257
00:23:54,850 --> 00:23:57,600
So your mom doesn’t like her
and wants them to break up.

258
00:23:58,360 --> 00:24:01,600
She asks Jay to steal Chan from Key.

259
00:24:02,150 --> 00:24:03,000
Right?

260
00:24:05,510 --> 00:24:08,800
Your lives are so tangled.

261
00:24:09,050 --> 00:24:10,960
Why can’t you do things the easy way?

262
00:24:11,280 --> 00:24:15,000
Things should have been over
if Jay didn’t come back.

263
00:24:16,650 --> 00:24:20,380
Jay may not be a very nice person.

264
00:24:21,170 --> 00:24:22,700
But I do feel sorry for her.

265
00:24:25,210 --> 00:24:26,380
Why?

266
00:24:27,610 --> 00:24:30,600
If I tell you,
you will say I take her side.

267
00:24:31,230 --> 00:24:34,500
Jay was guilt-tripped
into breaking up with Chan

268
00:24:35,050 --> 00:24:36,810
and marrying the American millionaire.

269
00:24:37,680 --> 00:24:39,520
Jay’s aunt had a financial problem.

270
00:24:40,330 --> 00:24:41,700
She was going to go bankrupt.

271
00:24:42,570 --> 00:24:46,490
Marrying that man was the only way
for her to save her family.

272
00:24:49,230 --> 00:24:50,700
You are Phu, right?

273
00:24:50,890 --> 00:24:52,000
I’m Elle.

274
00:24:52,930 --> 00:24:53,600
Yes.

275
00:24:55,220 --> 00:24:56,290
Can you do me a favor?

276
00:24:57,200 --> 00:24:58,370
What do you want me to do?

277
00:24:59,560 --> 00:25:00,300
Right.

278
00:25:01,240 --> 00:25:02,500
What are you going to do?

279
00:25:03,680 --> 00:25:05,050
I’m going to help you.

280
00:25:53,160 --> 00:25:54,300
Thank you.

281
00:25:56,620 --> 00:25:57,800
Are you feeling better?

282
00:26:07,930 --> 00:26:09,430
It’s unbelievable

283
00:26:13,020 --> 00:26:15,800
that you saved me both times.

284
00:26:19,570 --> 00:26:21,100
How did you know

285
00:26:22,760 --> 00:26:24,300
that I’m here?

286
00:26:28,580 --> 00:26:29,800
I didn’t know.

287
00:26:31,800 --> 00:26:33,670
But I had a hunch that you might be here.

288
00:26:35,940 --> 00:26:37,750
This is the place where we first met.

289
00:26:44,040 --> 00:26:45,100
That’s right.

290
00:26:47,650 --> 00:26:48,830
This place,

291
00:26:50,600 --> 00:26:52,100
it’s where I met you.

292
00:26:55,640 --> 00:26:57,300
I thought…

293
00:26:59,590 --> 00:27:03,300
this place might help me heal.

294
00:27:05,700 --> 00:27:07,400
Why didn’t you tell me?

295
00:27:11,480 --> 00:27:13,000
I could help you.

296
00:27:20,820 --> 00:27:22,400
I didn’t want you…

297
00:27:24,120 --> 00:27:26,900
to see me when I was falling apart.

298
00:27:29,780 --> 00:27:31,050
So…

299
00:27:32,810 --> 00:27:34,360
I ran away to be alone.

300
00:27:46,900 --> 00:27:50,890
Tonight, the moon looks scary.

301
00:27:57,710 --> 00:27:59,550
Some people believe that

302
00:28:01,740 --> 00:28:04,070
a lunar eclipse is a bad sign.

303
00:28:07,770 --> 00:28:09,300
But for me,

304
00:28:12,440 --> 00:28:14,700
it’s just a natural phenomenon

305
00:28:17,360 --> 00:28:21,100
when Earth casts a shadow on the Moon.

306
00:28:23,100 --> 00:28:24,600
It won’t last long.

307
00:28:26,610 --> 00:28:27,900
And it will pass.

308
00:28:48,770 --> 00:28:50,700
Just like bad things
that happened in the past,

309
00:28:53,460 --> 00:28:54,750
in the end,

310
00:28:56,570 --> 00:28:58,200
it will just be a thing of the past.

311
00:29:13,420 --> 00:29:15,000
But I’m still afraid.

312
00:29:17,180 --> 00:29:18,240
It’s dark.

313
00:29:21,650 --> 00:29:24,270
I like it better
when the moon shines brightly.

314
00:29:42,970 --> 00:29:44,900
♪ There may be nights ♪

315
00:29:47,000 --> 00:29:50,250
♪ when there’s no moon in the sky ♪

316
00:29:55,860 --> 00:30:03,800
♪ Days when my heart feels
far too tired to try ♪

317
00:30:07,710 --> 00:30:15,080
♪ But somehow time led you into my life ♪

318
00:30:16,960 --> 00:30:21,170
♪ You unlocked the empty space ♪

319
00:30:22,620 --> 00:30:26,600
♪ and let me love you right ♪

320
00:30:31,580 --> 00:30:37,670
♪ Feels just like a dream
that I found you ♪

321
00:30:41,080 --> 00:30:47,200
♪ Every second spent with you
is so meaningful ♪

322
00:30:50,080 --> 00:30:52,600
♪ The night shines bright, ♪

323
00:30:54,660 --> 00:30:58,600
♪ no words could ever do ♪

324
00:31:00,410 --> 00:31:04,030
♪ I know that it’s you ♪

325
00:31:18,400 --> 00:31:23,670
♪ The word “love” I say to you, ♪

326
00:31:26,440 --> 00:31:29,800
♪ I say it to you ♪

327
00:31:32,330 --> 00:31:38,400
♪ You’re the shining light
when no stars are coming through ♪

328
00:31:43,400 --> 00:31:54,400
♪ You’re the key
that found its way to my heart ♪

329
00:31:56,640 --> 00:32:04,450
♪ Let me love you, love you ♪

330
00:32:11,710 --> 00:32:16,450
Thank you for saving me.

331
00:33:10,780 --> 00:33:12,100
So pretty.

332
00:33:13,110 --> 00:33:14,600
Whose girlfriend is this?

333
00:33:16,490 --> 00:33:17,800
Your girlfriend.

334
00:33:19,650 --> 00:33:20,600
Chan.

335
00:33:21,470 --> 00:33:22,600
You’re up?

336
00:33:23,180 --> 00:33:24,600
Why didn’t you tell me?

337
00:33:27,490 --> 00:33:29,220
I want to cuddle you a bit longer.

338
00:33:33,170 --> 00:33:34,700
Doesn’t your arm hurt?

339
00:33:38,730 --> 00:33:40,600
If it means I get to hold you,

340
00:33:41,720 --> 00:33:42,900
it’s totally worth it.

341
00:34:03,680 --> 00:34:05,700
This is more than cuddling.

342
00:34:09,580 --> 00:34:13,610
Who did you learn
this naughty behavior from?

343
00:34:16,690 --> 00:34:18,000
Do you really need to ask that?

344
00:34:21,679 --> 00:34:23,360
When you become close to someone,

345
00:34:25,370 --> 00:34:26,949
you will pick up some of their behaviors.

346
00:34:28,050 --> 00:34:29,230
That’s normal.

347
00:34:31,110 --> 00:34:33,100
But I didn’t pick up
any of your behaviors.

348
00:34:34,250 --> 00:34:35,900
I guess we are not close enough.

349
00:34:56,190 --> 00:34:58,100
Is this close enough?

350
00:35:04,180 --> 00:35:05,400
Thank you

351
00:35:09,350 --> 00:35:11,400
for holding me through the night.

352
00:35:14,490 --> 00:35:16,770
I slept soundly
and didn’t have any nightmares.

353
00:35:17,810 --> 00:35:21,900
I will hold you any time you want.

354
00:36:02,640 --> 00:36:03,400
Come on.

355
00:36:03,950 --> 00:36:04,900
Let’s go home.

356
00:36:06,980 --> 00:36:07,700
Right.

357
00:36:08,380 --> 00:36:10,230
Simba must really miss me.

358
00:36:10,520 --> 00:36:11,450
That’s true.

359
00:36:12,730 --> 00:36:14,600
Let’s go home to our son.

360
00:36:18,700 --> 00:36:20,200
I like what you said.

361
00:36:22,950 --> 00:36:23,900
Why?

362
00:36:25,770 --> 00:36:30,200
It’s like I have my own family.

363
00:36:31,630 --> 00:36:37,470
There are Mama, Mommy, and our son, Simba.

364
00:36:42,420 --> 00:36:44,300
Let’s hurry home.

365
00:36:44,680 --> 00:36:48,280
Our son must be yowling nonstop.

366
00:36:51,990 --> 00:36:52,760
Come on.

367
00:36:53,100 --> 00:36:54,050
Thank you.

368
00:37:29,840 --> 00:37:30,700
Sun.

369
00:37:31,460 --> 00:37:32,900
What are you doing here, sweetie?

370
00:37:34,030 --> 00:37:35,330
I came to help Chan with her work.

371
00:37:36,630 --> 00:37:37,900
She’s busy.

372
00:37:38,500 --> 00:37:39,590
You?

373
00:37:41,210 --> 00:37:42,630
Yes, Mom.

374
00:37:43,130 --> 00:37:46,120
I know the work process of our hotel.

375
00:37:46,700 --> 00:37:49,900
She taught me
in case something like this happens.

376
00:37:50,980 --> 00:37:52,400
When did you learn it?

377
00:37:53,950 --> 00:37:56,490
I never knew that you were
interested in running our business.

378
00:37:56,830 --> 00:37:59,980
Miss Sun doesn’t want Miss Chan
to handle the hotel management alone.

379
00:38:00,460 --> 00:38:02,850
She often came in to learn
about the business when she had time.

380
00:38:04,100 --> 00:38:05,000
That’s right.

381
00:38:08,650 --> 00:38:10,770
These twins seem to really
love each other.

382
00:38:11,330 --> 00:38:13,100
Of course.

383
00:38:13,370 --> 00:38:15,100
We are twins.

384
00:38:16,250 --> 00:38:21,840
Whatever or whoever Chan loves,
I will love them too.

385
00:38:22,020 --> 00:38:23,000
Is that right?

386
00:38:26,960 --> 00:38:28,300
But I’m her mom.

387
00:38:29,440 --> 00:38:31,850
I love her and mean well to her.

388
00:38:34,310 --> 00:38:37,450
There are some things that people your age
might not have thought about.

389
00:38:38,150 --> 00:38:40,400
I’m older.
I should warn you about it, right?

390
00:38:43,380 --> 00:38:47,440
Warning us out of concern
and forcing us to do what you want,

391
00:38:48,290 --> 00:38:50,100
these are two different things, Mom.

392
00:38:57,610 --> 00:39:01,250
Are all kids these days such backtalkers?

393
00:39:22,730 --> 00:39:24,300
Simba, where are you?

394
00:39:24,750 --> 00:39:26,100
Mommy is back.

395
00:39:30,590 --> 00:39:32,300
Do you miss me?

396
00:39:32,460 --> 00:39:33,690
I’m sorry.

397
00:39:33,730 --> 00:39:35,000
I’m back now.

398
00:39:40,180 --> 00:39:41,500
Do you remember Mommy?

399
00:39:43,600 --> 00:39:45,100
Are you mad at me?

400
00:39:46,350 --> 00:39:48,500
Don’t leave your son again.

401
00:39:52,480 --> 00:39:56,000
Simba, I’m not leaving you again.

402
00:39:57,690 --> 00:39:58,500
Right?

403
00:39:59,980 --> 00:40:01,500
Don’t leave Mama too.

404
00:40:05,660 --> 00:40:08,100
Why have you never patted me on the head?

405
00:40:17,350 --> 00:40:19,440
Why is this cat not meowing?

406
00:40:21,090 --> 00:40:22,600
I’m a human.

407
00:40:30,230 --> 00:40:33,810
Our family is warm.

408
00:40:36,250 --> 00:40:37,180
Right?

409
00:40:42,540 --> 00:40:43,330
Key.

410
00:40:45,150 --> 00:40:46,400
Tonight,

411
00:40:47,490 --> 00:40:49,000
let’s go to your family’s house.

412
00:41:05,670 --> 00:41:06,530
Don’t worry.

413
00:41:10,220 --> 00:41:11,800
I’ll always be by your side.

414
00:41:34,750 --> 00:41:36,200
Hello, Aunt Niam.

415
00:41:37,370 --> 00:41:38,680
Take off your shoes here.

416
00:41:38,720 --> 00:41:39,800
Thank you.

417
00:41:40,000 --> 00:41:41,330
Put the slippers on.

418
00:41:47,310 --> 00:41:48,200
Hello.

419
00:41:48,680 --> 00:41:49,900
I’m back.

420
00:42:03,280 --> 00:42:05,200
I’m sorry that I worried you.

421
00:42:09,150 --> 00:42:10,300
It’s alright, sweeties.

422
00:42:10,440 --> 00:42:13,600
Just seeing you come back safely
is good enough for me.

423
00:42:19,600 --> 00:42:21,900
Thank you for taking her home.

424
00:42:23,090 --> 00:42:24,100
You’re welcome.

425
00:42:30,290 --> 00:42:31,290
Big Mom.

426
00:42:32,670 --> 00:42:33,600
Dad.

427
00:42:35,990 --> 00:42:36,810
Aunt Niam.

428
00:42:37,400 --> 00:42:38,250
Yes.

429
00:42:39,760 --> 00:42:44,000
This is Chan, my girlfriend.

430
00:42:48,400 --> 00:42:49,500
Miss Key.

431
00:42:49,910 --> 00:42:52,550
We’ve known it for some time.

432
00:42:53,680 --> 00:42:55,110
We saw the news.

433
00:42:55,150 --> 00:42:57,610
Miss Peach also told us

434
00:42:57,650 --> 00:43:01,500
about your photoshoot celebrating
your two-week anniversary of dating.

435
00:43:02,160 --> 00:43:04,780
-You know all the details.
-Of course.

436
00:43:07,140 --> 00:43:13,190
This is an official
introduction of her to my family.

437
00:43:27,310 --> 00:43:28,500
Chan, do you know this?

438
00:43:29,450 --> 00:43:32,300
There was a time when Key was young,

439
00:43:32,670 --> 00:43:35,560
she went outside
and watched the moon every night.

440
00:43:36,280 --> 00:43:39,100
Sometimes, she fell asleep outside.

441
00:43:40,250 --> 00:43:44,010
And you would carry me back
to my bed every time.

442
00:43:45,990 --> 00:43:48,100
Now, you have a girlfriend named Chan.

443
00:43:48,650 --> 00:43:50,040
This must be destiny.

444
00:44:00,710 --> 00:44:01,700
Key, honey.

445
00:44:02,640 --> 00:44:03,910
Actually,

446
00:44:04,760 --> 00:44:06,970
I have something to talk to you two about.

447
00:44:12,320 --> 00:44:13,400
What is it?

448
00:44:15,790 --> 00:44:21,900
Chan, do you know about Key’s mom
and her and Key’s status in the family?

449
00:44:23,330 --> 00:44:24,350
Dad.

450
00:44:25,730 --> 00:44:28,150
I want you to know that

451
00:44:28,920 --> 00:44:31,000
I’ve never thought less of Key.

452
00:44:32,980 --> 00:44:34,000
I know.

453
00:44:34,950 --> 00:44:37,600
But I want to explain
so you two will understand.

454
00:44:43,630 --> 00:44:47,300
Your mom loved you very much.

455
00:44:48,640 --> 00:44:50,390
Because of her illness,

456
00:44:51,850 --> 00:44:55,000
she did things that hurt you.

457
00:45:03,010 --> 00:45:04,130
I know.

458
00:45:08,150 --> 00:45:10,500
Every time she hurt me without meaning to,

459
00:45:12,100 --> 00:45:13,600
she always regretted it.

460
00:45:18,380 --> 00:45:19,670
I loved her.

461
00:45:22,440 --> 00:45:24,000
I never hated her.

462
00:45:28,540 --> 00:45:30,000
I know she was sick.

463
00:45:39,510 --> 00:45:41,980
I was the one
who made her condition worse.

464
00:45:43,980 --> 00:45:45,300
It was my fault.

465
00:45:47,960 --> 00:45:50,230
It was because of my incompetence.

466
00:45:51,520 --> 00:45:54,600
I was secretly dating her

467
00:45:55,690 --> 00:45:57,200
when we were in school.

468
00:45:59,210 --> 00:46:00,700
My dad,

469
00:46:03,800 --> 00:46:06,300
he forced me to marry Big Mom.

470
00:46:10,650 --> 00:46:13,300
I did something selfish.

471
00:46:18,550 --> 00:46:20,300
I hurt everyone.

472
00:46:24,400 --> 00:46:28,900
Big Mom was really nice to me.

473
00:46:33,990 --> 00:46:35,450
I never thought

474
00:46:39,500 --> 00:46:42,080
that I would fall in love with her
because of her goodness.

475
00:46:42,970 --> 00:46:45,100
I ended up hurting your mom so badly

476
00:46:46,730 --> 00:46:48,100
that she got ill.

477
00:46:55,610 --> 00:46:57,600
I was a terrible man.

478
00:46:59,540 --> 00:47:01,500
I couldn’t do anything…

479
00:47:04,450 --> 00:47:09,300
to help your mom or you.

480
00:47:16,710 --> 00:47:17,750
I’m sorry.

481
00:47:27,590 --> 00:47:28,600
Dad.

482
00:47:32,660 --> 00:47:35,200
You’re the best dad to me.

483
00:47:44,770 --> 00:47:45,950
From now on,

484
00:47:47,160 --> 00:47:49,000
you need to stop blaming yourself.

485
00:47:50,420 --> 00:47:51,470
Do you hear me?

486
00:48:22,930 --> 00:48:24,470
Thank you, Dad.

487
00:48:49,000 --> 00:48:49,850
Chan.

488
00:48:54,550 --> 00:48:56,500
Are we really going to sleep over here?

489
00:49:00,640 --> 00:49:01,400
Yes.

490
00:49:02,820 --> 00:49:04,150
Let’s sleep over here.

491
00:49:04,900 --> 00:49:06,600
I want to see how you lived.

492
00:49:34,770 --> 00:49:35,500
Key.

493
00:49:36,500 --> 00:49:37,370
Yes.

494
00:49:37,790 --> 00:49:38,800
Are you okay?

495
00:49:47,090 --> 00:49:48,000
Let’s go.

496
00:50:25,670 --> 00:50:26,920
You can’t sleep?

497
00:50:31,180 --> 00:50:31,960
Yes.

498
00:50:47,150 --> 00:50:48,150
Are you afraid?

499
00:50:55,100 --> 00:50:56,940
I’m afraid that if I fall asleep,

500
00:50:59,490 --> 00:51:01,250
I will have a nightmare about my mom.

501
00:51:03,340 --> 00:51:05,050
I don’t want to see it again.

502
00:51:10,680 --> 00:51:12,050
If you don’t want
to have the nightmare again,

503
00:51:13,130 --> 00:51:15,100
why don’t we face it together?

504
00:52:41,520 --> 00:52:44,570
The doctor said that
if I have someone I love,

505
00:52:44,610 --> 00:52:45,920
it will help my healing.

506
00:52:45,960 --> 00:52:47,970
I already have one. That’s you.

507
00:52:48,080 --> 00:52:51,900
I don’t get
why Chan loves Key that much.

508
00:52:51,930 --> 00:52:54,140
That’s Chan’s business.
It’s no longer yours.

509
00:52:54,420 --> 00:52:55,930
Mom, are you going to sleep over here?

510
00:52:56,140 --> 00:52:56,710
Why?

511
00:52:56,750 --> 00:52:58,300
Are you going to tell me to leave again?

512
00:52:58,910 --> 00:53:00,610
I’m not feeling well today.

513
00:53:00,750 --> 00:53:01,690
I think I’m sick.

514
00:53:01,900 --> 00:53:03,330
Do you want me to stay
and take care of you?

515
00:53:03,360 --> 00:53:04,840
If you have nothing else to do.

516
00:53:04,850 --> 00:53:06,530
No problem, Mom.

517
00:53:07,360 --> 00:53:09,000
Oops, I mean, Madam.

518
00:53:09,090 --> 00:53:11,170
All we do is
display our hatred to each other.

519
00:53:11,370 --> 00:53:12,530
Don’t you feel bad for Chan?

520
00:53:12,730 --> 00:53:15,100
Why do we have to hate each other?
